# Implementation Plan - Extreme Scale Stabilization & Real-time Visibility

This plan addresses the 1.8GB processing failure by removing Nginx bottlenecks, implementing real-time progress *during* the restore phase, and adding the requested dashboard cards.

## User Review Required

> [!CAUTION]
> **Large File Support**: I found that Nginx was blocking your 1.8gb upload because it had the default 1MB limit. I will increase this to 2GB and extend timeouts to 1 hour to ensure large transfers don't drop.
> 
> [!IMPORTANT]
> **Visibility Fix**: Currently, you only see tables *after* the SQL is fully loaded. For a 1.8GB file, this takes long enough to look like a hang. I will change the logic so that the dashboard updates **as the database is being populated**, showing you tables appearing in real-time even during the "Restoring" phase.

## Proposed Changes

### 1. Infrastructure (Nginx & API Timeout)

#### [MODIFY] [nginx.conf](file:///home/eisen/Downloads/SQAuto/docker/nginx.conf)
- Add `client_max_body_size 2G;`.
- Increase `proxy_read_timeout`, `proxy_connect_timeout`, and `send_timeout` to `3600` (1 hour).

### 2. Backend - Real-time Progress Monitoring

#### [MODIFY] [service.py](file:///home/eisen/Downloads/SQAuto/services/dump_restore/service.py)
- Refactor the `restore` method to run `psql` as a background process (`subprocess.Popen`).
- Add a "Watcher" loop that queries the database every 10 seconds to see which tables have appeared.
- Update `Job.profile` incrementally during the restore so the UI stays alive and interactive.

#### [MODIFY] [service.py](file:///home/eisen/Downloads/SQAuto/services/schema_profiler/service.py)
- Implement a more detailed "Data Statistics" gatherer to populate the new cards:
    - **Total Rows**: Sum of all rows across detected tables.
    - **Data Size**: Size of the staging database in MB.
    - **Duplicates**: Analyze table indices/keys to estimate duplicate counts.

### 3. UI - 5-Card Dashboard

#### [MODIFY] [page.tsx](file:///home/eisen/Downloads/SQAuto/apps/web/src/app/page.tsx)
- Update the layout to display 5 cards: **TABLES**, **ROWS**, **DATA EXTRACTED**, **DUPLICATE DATA**, and **READINESS**.
- Enhance the polling logic to handle "Restoring" as a live-update state.

#### [MODIFY] [SummaryCard.tsx](file:///home/eisen/Downloads/SQAuto/apps/web/src/components/SummaryCard.tsx)
- Ensure all 5 cards fit elegantly in the grid.

## Open Questions

- **Timeout Warning**: Is 1 hour enough for your largest files, or should we set it to unlimited? (Unlimited carries a small security risk of hung connections on the VM).
- **Duplicate Logic**: For "Duplicate Data", do you have a specific definition (e.g., identical primary keys)? Or should I use a generic check for "Possible Duplicates" based on repeated values?

## Verification Plan

### Automated Tests
- `curl -I -X POST -F "file=@large.sql" https://sqauto.zeraynce.com/api/upload` -> Verify 201 Created for 1.8GB file.
- Inspect logs for "Watcher: Found X tables during restore".

### Manual Verification
- Perform a 1GB+ scan and capture a recording showing the "TABLES" and "ROWS" cards counting up LIVE während the restore phase.
